gned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+{x}_{3}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -22\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=-22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 5 & -22\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 5 & -22\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the reduced matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=2,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=-6,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n2\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+0\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+(-6)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -22\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2+0+(-6)=-4.$" 13194139533577 17592186045417 true] [17592186409635 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409633 13194139533577 17592186045417 true] [17592186409635 1069 "q-74970" 13194139533577 17592186045417 true] [17592186409635 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533577 17592186045417 true] [17592186409635 1071 "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis of $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ by inspection." 13194139533577 17592186045417 true] [17592186409635 1072 #uuid "60af0127-6c17-5939-bada-d5e4db0c560b" 13194139533577 17592186045417 true] [17592186409635 1074 "Remember that a basis of $S$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that spans $S.$\n\nFrom the given vectors, we can see that ${a}_{2}$ is a linear combination of vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=1\\cdot {a}_{1}+1\\cdot {a}_{3}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the vector ${a}_{2}$ can be removed from $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ without changing the span. So $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is spanned by just ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}.$ \n\nLastly, note that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent since they are not parallel. So the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set that spans $S.$\n\nTherefore, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}},{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}}.\n$$" 13194139533577 17592186045417 true] [17592186409636 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409631 13194139533577 17592186045417 true] [17592186409636 1069 "q-76329" 13194139533577 17592186045417 true] [17592186409636 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533577 17592186045417 true] [17592186409636 1071 "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are given below. Determine whether $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${a}_{3}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533577 17592186045417 true] [17592186409636 1072 #uuid "c63eedb8-35fe-5b46-b979-91cc24ab9428" 13194139533577 17592186045417 true] [17592186409636 1074 "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=14 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 14 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the RREF matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-5,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n2\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+(-5)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2\\cdot (-5)=-10.$" 13194139533577 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-2d2fc535-0009-527e-8e16-197236ba5926" 17592186409616 "answer-3a46ae99-d148-5f19-94ba-416fdd09e06f" 17592186409617 "answer-5aaf6733-e757-5737-a6d7-d37f344e2387" 17592186409618 "answer-6536472f-623b-557c-ba85-a0b19e98cf60" 17592186409619 "answer-8e0cb693-c1d6-5a53-a944-ae0f4704df17" 